('venue-strike-bowling-king-street-wharf', 'editorial_summary', '"Strike offers whole-venue exclusive hire including the lanes, a private bar, arcade games and other activities, with a personal host and a pizza-and-burger style menu. Its own page lists birthdays, engagements and celebratory bashes but never says weddings, so a wedding enquiry should be confirmed first. Harbour-side King Street Wharf is the best-placed site for a casual celebration; the group''s other Sydney sites follow the same model."'::jsonb, 'known', 0.8, 'primary_official', 'https://strikebowling.com.au/parties/exclusive-hire', 'Unconventional venues import 2026-11-05', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-11-05 00:00:00+00', NULL),
('venue-strike-bowling-king-street-wharf', 'capacity_seated_max', '80'::jsonb, 'known', 0.8, 'primary_official', 'https://strikebowling.com.au/parties/exclusive-hire', 'Unconventional venues import 2026-11-05', TIMESTAMPTZ '2026-11-05 00:00:00+00', 'The Darling Harbour location page says the venue seats up to 80 people including front bar tables and the outdoor area. The exclusive-hire page says each venue differs in size and that maximum capacity is shown during booking, so standing capacity is not published. Other NSW Strike sites on the same exclusive-hire programme: Macquarie Centre, 4 Waterloo Rd, North Ryde NSW 2113; Mandarin Centre, Level 4/65 Albert Ave, Chatswood NSW 2067; Alexandria; Entertainment Quarter (207/122 Lang Rd, Sydney NSW 2021); Castle Hill; Penrith; Charlestown; Wollongong. They share one enquiry form and have no separate contact details, so they are covered by this single record.'),
